  "content": {
    "id": "p11-q20-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Find the three-digit number that increases by 20% when 1 is added to each of its digits.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$555$.\n\nAdding 1 to each digit increases the number by $111$, which is $20\\%$ of the original.",
      "worked": "Let the digits be $A$, $B$ and $C$, and let $N=100A+10B+C$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}100(A+1)+10(B+1)+(C+1)&=100A+10B+C+111\\\\100(A+1)+10(B+1)+(C+1)&=N+111.\\end{align*}$$\n\nA $20\\%$ increase has multiplier $1.2$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N+111&=1.2N\\\\111&=0.2N\\\\N&=\\frac{111}{0.2}\\\\N&=555.\\end{align*}$$\n\nCheck: adding 1 to each digit gives $666$, and $1.2\\times555=666$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 76
  },
